cartridge "RAGING THUNDER/BY CRAIG M. BUCK RUN 92/1992"

' RAGING THUNDER - ColecoVision port of "Raging Thunder" by Craig M. Buck,
' RUN Magazine, ReRUN disk March/April 1992 side B (Commodore 64, BASIC +
' machine code MLRAGE.OBJ / MLACTN.OBJ). Rules from the article on the
' disk (rage.txt) and from the disassembled machine code (orig/).
'
' The game: your submarine hunts the Night Wolf fleet (submarines,
' battleships, aircraft carriers) in a wrap-around tactical box. Enemy
' vessels are only seen inside your naval radar range (35 units around the
' sub); a vessel inside that range knows where you are and hunts you, and
' fires a THUNDR-5 when it faces you (one hit sinks you). Surfacing or
' switching the radar on also gives your position away; the radar shows the
' aircraft, and aircraft can only drop depth charges on a sub that is
' above 400 ft while its radar is on (two charges sink you). Carriers
' launch helicopters, jets fly by at random. Torpedoes: STINGER 1 point of
' damage, THUNDR-5 2 points, SAM 1 point (helicopters only). A submarine
' sinks after 2 points, a carrier 3, a battleship 4. You cannot fire below
' 400 ft. Sink the whole fleet to win. Six fleets (levels) and six game
' speeds (1 fastest), as in the original.
'
' Controls (controller 1 or 2):
'   stick left/right   turn 45 degrees          stick up/down  speed +/- 10 kn
'   button 1           fire the loaded tube
'   button 2 held +    stick down: dive / stop, up: climb / stop,
'                      left: load the next weapon, right: radar on/off
'   keypad shortcuts (the original's keys): 1 dive, 2 climb, 3 THUNDR-5,
'   4 STINGER, 5 SAM, 0 empty the tube, 7 radar, * / # crosshair range
'
' Timing (measured in jsc64): one "sub-tick" every 6 frames moves aircraft
' and enemy torpedoes; one game tick every SPEED sub-ticks moves the subs,
' the vessels, your torpedoes and the depth (speed 6 = 0.6 s a tick).
'
' Liberties (ColecoVision adaptation): title menu with LEVEL/SPEED, HOW TO
' PLAY and CREDITS instead of the C64 action menu; joystick + 2 buttons
' instead of keys (keypad keeps the original numbers); the crosshair is on
' whenever a tube is loaded (no separate "8" key); battle scenes are new
' side-view pictures; colours and sprites are new.
' Original bugs fixed: the enemy's wander target used the y range for x
' and the x range for y (it could circle for ever); two diagonal wraps of
' the enemy were broken; a shot with both torpedo slots busy wasted the
' ammunition; a jet's depth-charge check read the wrong variable (it hit
' at any depth); an aircraft could hit again after its charge; the SAM in
' the second slot could not hit a helicopter. No score (the original has
' none): you win or lose against the fleet.

